# LUXE Store — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun install && bun run db:setup && bun run dev
# db:setup = `prisma db push` + seed (idempotent — safe to re-run).

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default. The `db/` folder lives at the repo root (git-ignored).
# A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against prisma/schema.prisma — exactly
# like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db` points at <repo>/db/custom.db
# for the CLI (push/seed), `next build`, and the running server alike,
# regardless of the process working directory. (src/lib/db-path.ts implements
# this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts pins the contract.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is recommended — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — used for metadata, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt.
# Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret for the `luxe_session` cookie (HMAC).
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Email verification (session-4) ----------------------------------------
# Reference-parity machinery for the post-signup "Verify your email" flow.
# OFF by default: no transactional email provider is wired (codes log at the
# console seam), and an always-on gate would lock new users out. Flip to
# "true" once an email provider is connected — registration then requires
# the 6-digit code and unverified logins are blocked (reference behavior).
AUTH_REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=""
